{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For not.</b> Some interpret: if the great good does not endure for him, he will remember the days of his life in which he enjoyed himself, and in their remembrance he has joy of heart. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is: thus he will remember, for not many are the days of his life. And the <i>et</i> is superfluous, like 'and the lion came, and the bear' (1 Samuel 17:34)." "<b>For Elohim answers.</b> Its meaning is 'provides,' like 'I will answer the heavens and they will answer the earth' (Hosea 2:23–24). And some say it is from the root ענה, and its meaning is: he answers the one who asks and seeks according to his request, and likewise he answers all. And מענה is from the intensive binyan, added upon the pattern of מעלה, נשיאים. And the meaning is that HaShem assists him in his joy, for He gave it to him and empowered him to eat of it. And the meaning of 'of it' [ממנו] is that it is not fitting that he eat of it excessively."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "Reading משקל מעלה נשיאים as three nouns illustrating the nominal pattern; the phrase is compressed and the grammatical point opaque."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:54.181651607Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}